---
import BaseLayout from '@layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '@lib/site';

const lastUpdated = 'May 2025';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How Ember & Ink collects, uses, and protects your data — including cookies, analytics, forms, and your rights under GDPR and CCPA."
  url={`${SITE.url}/privacy/`}
>
  <article class="container-ember py-16 md:py-24 max-w-3xl">
    <header>
      <p class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-muted">
        The legal bits
      </p>
      <h1 class="mt-3 text-4xl md:text-5xl text-burgundy">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-muted">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>
      <p class="mt-6 text-muted">
        Ember &amp; Ink ("we", "us", "our") operates {SITE.url}. This page
        explains what we collect, why we collect it, and the choices you
        have. We keep this policy short and accurate — if a tool is not
        listed here, we are not using it.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="prose-ember mt-10">
      <h2>1. The short version</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>We do not sell your personal information.</li>
        <li>We do not run advertising networks or tracking pixels.</li>
        <li>
          We use privacy-friendly analytics only after you explicitly
          consent.
        </li>
        <li>
          If you contact us or subscribe to the newsletter, we store only
          what you send us, and only for that purpose.
        </li>
        <li>
          Amazon affiliate links open on Amazon's site, which has its own
          privacy policy.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>2. What we collect</h2>
      <h3>a. Analytics data (only with your consent)</h3>
      <p>
        If you accept analytics via the cookie banner, we load Google
        Analytics 4 (GA4). GA4 collects aggregated data such as your
        approximate location (country/region), device type, browser,
        referring site, and the pages you visit. We configure GA4 with
        <strong>IP anonymisation enabled</strong>. GA4 sets cookies on
        your device once you have consented. You can withdraw consent at
        any time using the "Cookie settings" link in the footer.
      </p>

      <h3>b. Information you send us directly</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Contact form</strong> — your name, email, and message
          (only if you fill out the form).
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Newsletter signup</strong> — your email address (only if
          you subscribe).
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Email</strong> — anything you send to
          <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        We use this information solely to reply to you, or to send you
        the newsletter you signed up for. We do not share or sell it.
      </p>

      <h3>c. Standard server logs</h3>
      <p>
        Like almost every website, our host (Cloudflare Pages) records
        basic technical information such as IP address, timestamp, and
        requested URL for security and abuse-prevention purposes. These
        logs are retained by Cloudflare under their own privacy policy
        and are not connected to any other data we hold.
      </p>

      <h2>3. Cookies and consent</h2>
      <p>
        We use two categories of cookies/storage:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Essential storage</strong> — a single
          <code>localStorage</code> key (<code>ember-consent-v1</code>)
          that remembers your cookie choice. No personal data.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Analytics cookies</strong> — only if you click "Accept
          all" on the consent banner. These are Google Analytics 4 cookies
          (typically <code>_ga</code> and <code>_ga_*</code>).
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        If you click "Essential only", no analytics cookies are set and GA4
        is never loaded. You can change your choice at any time via the
        "Cookie settings" link in the footer.
      </p>

      <h2>4. Third parties we use</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Cloudflare Pages</strong> — hosting and CDN.
          <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" rel="noopener" target="_blank">
            Cloudflare privacy policy
          </a>.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Google Analytics 4</strong> — aggregated site analytics,
          only with consent.
          <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="noopener" target="_blank">
            Google privacy policy
          </a>.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Amazon Associates</strong> — affiliate links open on
          Amazon.
          <a href="https://www.amazon.com/gp/help/customer/display.html?nodeId=468496" rel="noopener" target="_blank">
            Amazon privacy notice
          </a>.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Formspree</strong> (or equivalent form backend) — only
          if you submit the contact or newsletter form. Form data is
          delivered to our inbox and is not stored on this site.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>5. Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        Depending on where you live, you may have the right to access,
        correct, export, or delete the personal information we hold about
        you, and to withdraw consent for analytics at any time.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>GDPR (EU/UK/Swiss)</strong> — you have the right to
          request a copy of your data, ask us to delete it, and object to
          processing. Our lawful basis for analytics is your explicit
          consent; for contact/newsletter, it is your request and our
          legitimate interest in replying.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>CCPA (California)</strong> — you have the right to know
          what personal information we collect, to request its deletion,
          and to opt out of its sale. We do not sell personal
          information.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        To exercise any of these rights, email
        <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>. We respond
        within 30 days.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Data retention</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Contact form submissions and newsletter signups: retained until
          you ask us to delete them, or (for the newsletter) until you
          unsubscribe.
        </li>
        <li>
          Analytics data: retained for the default GA4 period configured
          in our property (currently 14 months).
        </li>
        <li>
          Server logs: retained by Cloudflare under their standard policy.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>7. Children</h2>
      <p>
        Ember &amp; Ink is not directed at children under 13. We do not
        knowingly collect personal information from children. If you
        believe a child has submitted information to us, please contact
        us and we will delete it.
      </p>

      <h2>8. Security</h2>
      <p>
        We serve the site over HTTPS, apply strict security headers
        (including a Content Security Policy), and only load third-party
        scripts strictly necessary for the site to work. No system is
        perfectly secure, but we work to keep the attack surface small.
      </p>

      <h2>9. Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>
        If we make material changes, we will update the "Last updated"
        date at the top of this page. Continued use of the site after
        changes constitutes acceptance of the updated policy.
      </p>

      <h2>10. Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about privacy? Email
        <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a> or use the
        <a href="/contact/">contact form</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>